# Image Generator v2 — Final Consolidated Feedback (5-High)

Sources merged: reports/feedback_gemini.md, reports/feedback_gpt5codex.md, reports/feedback_gpt5high, reports/feedback_sonnet4.5.md

## Executive Summary
The app has a strong foundation (React + Vite + TS, TanStack Query, Supabase) with rich prompt/gallery workflows. To be production-ready, focus on five high-impact areas: security of data access and secrets, modularizing monolithic pages, consistent error handling and logging, performance of lists and image pipeline, and TypeScript strictness/testing. This document consolidates all findings and prescribes an actionable roadmap.

## Top 5 High‑Impact Priorities
1. Security and configuration hygiene
2. Page modularization and shared state/components
3. Error boundary, logging, and consistent user feedback
4. Data/query efficiency and list performance (virtualization, selective columns, indexes)
5. TypeScript strictness and testing baseline (Vitest + Playwright)

---

## Comprehensive Findings (Consolidated)

### Security & Compliance
- Supabase URL/key committed in source; inconsistent use of env validation in settings.ts.
- RLS overly permissive: public INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE on prompts/images; direct client writes with anon key.
- Destructive actions rely on window.confirm; no audit logging/role checks.

### Architecture & Code Quality
- Monolithic pages: Prompts.tsx (~900 lines) and Gallery.tsx (>1k) interleave data logic, UI, and side effects.
- Significant duplication between Prompts and Gallery (filters, pagination, selection, bulk actions).
- Shared filter state via localStorage can cause race conditions/cross-tab churn.
- Outdated/dead artifacts: obsolete Tasks route, backup/bak files, mixed package managers.

### Data & API Layer
- Broad select clauses and relational joins fetching more than rendered; client-side resorting post-ordered fetches.
- Bulk generation loops sequential, lacking throttling/abort/retry.
- Multiple storage backends (Firebase + inline base64 + provider URLs); Supabase Storage not leveraged.

### Type Safety, Error Handling, Logging
- TS config permissive (noImplicitAny=false, strictNullChecks=false, etc.).
- 60+ console statements; inconsistent error handling and user messaging; no global error boundary.

### Performance & UX
- Large lists render in full; missing virtualization, lazy image loading, skeletons.
- Gallery/Prompts filter on many columns without targeted DB indexes.
- Main-thread canvas conversions block UI; heavy synchronous uploads; pipeline doesn’t flip ready=true reliably.
- Filters panel dense; mobile/keyboard accessibility limited.

### Documentation & DevEx
- Docs vs code drift (Next.js mentions; dev port mismatch). No .env.example. Testing not configured. Console logging verbose; no adjustable levels.

